    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while the end-to-end flow still runs from image features to reconstruction.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes features, then those features are partitioned into windows without changing the carrier. The DQ-CTM stage repeats its thought update on that carrier, rather than sending control back to the encoder. The same DQ-CTM parameters are reused across ticks before the decoder produces the output.",
